ore_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.10677848190960594,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03593179909526532,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":40.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.07883,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":52.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Preferred Bank provides various banking products and services to small and mid-sized businesses, entrepreneurs, real estate developers, professionals, and high net worth individuals. The company accepts checking, savings, and money market deposit accounts; fixed-rate and fixed maturity retail, and non-retail certificates of deposit; and individual retirement accounts. It also provides real estate mortgage loans that are secured by retail, industrial, office, special purpose, and residential single and multi-family properties; real estate construction loans; commercial loans, including lines of credit for working capital, term loans for capital expenditures, and commercial and stand-by letters of credit; and small business administration loans for business purposes, such as owner-occupied commercial real estate, business acquisitions, start-ups, franchise financing, working capital, improvements and renovations, inventory and equipment, and debt-refinancing. In addition, the company offers trade finance services, including commercial and export letters of credit, import lines of credit, documentary collections, international wire transfers, acceptances/trust receipt financing, export financing, and bills purchase programs. Further, it provides cash management services; and internet, mobile, and tablet banking services. The company was incorporated in 1991 and is headquartered in Los Angeles, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Li  Yu | Chairman, CEO & Corporate Secretary | Age 84 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 324 people. Revenue per employee of $875K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $515K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $31K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Preferred Bank is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.2B market cap on $283M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","The business throws off $167M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 59 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.26\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 7.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (PFBC) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_PFBC_Price_Events_111326121401_1794546841.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794546841.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Preferred Bank (NASDAQ:PFBC) Stock Rated \u201cModerate Buy\u201d by Wall Street Brokerages","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/preferred-bank-nasdaqpfbc-stock-rated-moderate-buy-by-wall-street-brokerages.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794131938.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.832,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Preferred Bank (PFBC) Reports Mixed Results, Is It Still Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-pfbc/preferred-bank/news/preferred-bank-pfbc-reports-mixed-results-is-it-still-below","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":17941